":44,"y":6,"cargo":[9,9]},{"type":33,"x":44,"y":14},{"type":49,"x":43,"y":10}]}],"objective":{"kind":"destroyType","type":39,"edge":"west"},"general":{"x":14,"y":10},"turnLimit":18,"cap":9,"music":21,"briefing":"Hestia Minor is a lump of iron and ice with eleven thousand miners living under its west rim. Ruess worked here once. When the Directorate ordered the moon's ore ships turned into troop transports, the miners said no. Kessrin's answer is on its way.\n\nFour Hannibal assault cruisers, with escorts. Ships can't cross the plateau's bedrock, so they'll come up the two channels the mine cut through it, straight to the colony. If one of them reaches the west edge, the colony is gone.\n\nWe have Ruess's batteries. Two Dragons already stand on the mine railway, one over each channel. His Crab carries a Hydra, and our own Crabs can set more down anywhere on bedrock, asteroids or deck. Once a battery is down, it stays down. Choose the ground carefully.\n\nThe cruisers won't come alone. Expect landers on the plateau and bombers over it, in waves.","goal":"Destroy all four Hannibal assault cruisers before any of them reaches the colony on the west edge.","routes":[{"prio":1,"x":44,"y":5},{"prio":2,"x":41,"y":5},{"prio":3,"x":38,"y":5},{"prio":4,"x":35,"y":5},{"prio":5,"x":32,"y":5},{"prio":6,"x":29,"y":5},{"prio":7,"x":26,"y":5},{"prio":8,"x":23,"y":5},{"prio":9,"x":20,"y":5},{"prio":10,"x":17,"y":5},{"prio":11,"x":14,"y":5},{"prio":12,"x":11,"y":5},{"prio":13,"x":8,"y":5},{"prio":14,"x":5,"y":5},{"prio":15,"x":2,"y":5},{"prio":1,"x":44,"y":14},{"prio":2,"x":41,"y":14},{"prio":3,"x":38,"y":14},{"prio":4,"x":35,"y":14},{"prio":5,"x":32,"y":14},{"prio":6,"x":29,"y":14},{"prio":7,"x":26,"y":14},{"prio":8,"x":23,"y":14},{"prio":9,"x":20,"y":14},{"prio":10,"x":17,"y":14},{"prio":11,"x":14,"y":14},{"prio":12,"x":11,"y":14},{"prio":13,"x":8,"y":14},{"prio":14,"x":5,"y":14},{"prio":15,"x":2,"y":14}],"chapter":"Chapter 4 · Hestia Minor","strategy":["The cruisers must come up the two channels (rows 5-6 and 14-15). Set batteries on the bedrock beside them, three to seven hexes in.","A Crab sets its battery down next to itself and the battery never moves again. Unload early, before the waves.","Kill the Hannibals; everything else only matters if it threatens a battery or the colony.","Landers come onto the plateau on turn 4, bombers on turn 7, a carrier group on turn 10. Keep mecha near the batteries.","The Selene and fast craft are the last line: stop any cruiser that slips through before it reaches the west edge."],"plan":[{"n":1,"path":[[38,5],[26,5],[8,5]]},{"n":1,"path":[[38,14],[26,14],[8,14]]},{"n":2,"at":[22,8],"note":"Battery ground"},{"n":2,"at":[22,12],"note":"Battery ground"},{"n":4,"at":[30,10],"note":"Landers, turn 4"},{"n":5,"at":[2,10],"note":"Colony"}],"comms":[{"speaker":"ruess","text":"A Dragon reaches seven hexes and hits like the end of the world, but it can't fire into a magnetic field and it can't move. Put them where the cruisers have to come, and they'll come."},{"speaker":"kessrin","text":"Eleven thousand miners, General. Their deaths will be on your ledger, not mine. You could still save them. Surrender the batteries."},{"speaker":"sato","text":"Selene will hold the north channel mouth. If a cruiser gets past the guns, I'm the last thing between it and the colony."},{"speaker":"arkin","text":"Landers on the plateau, bombers overhead, cruisers up the middle. Finally, a fair fight."}]}